<article class="env-remark" id="0GAX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GAX">Remark <span data-tag="0GAX">88.7.3</span>.</a> Let $I$ be an ideal of a Noetherian ring $A$. Let $B$ be an object of (<a href="/tag/0AL4" data-tag="0AL4">88.2.0.2</a>) which is rig-smooth over $(A, I)$. It is shown in <span class="cite">[<span class="postnote">Theorem 1.2</span>, <a href="/bibliography/gabber-zavyalov">gabber-zavyalov</a>]</span> that $B$ is isomorphic to the $I$-adic completion of a finite type $A$-algebra. This result supercedes the following list of partial results: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If $A$ is a G-ring, then the result follows from Proposition <a href="/tag/0GAT" data-tag="0GAT">88.6.3</a>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $B$ is rig-étale over $(A, I)$, then the result follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0AKA" data-tag="0AKA">88.10.2</a>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $I$ is principal, then the result follows from <span class="cite">[<span class="postnote">III Theorem 7</span>, <a href="/bibliography/Elkik">Elkik</a>]</span>. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>